  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member composing a new MP, I want the formatting bar to stay still above the keyboard instead of moving up and down. Part of #592, under umbrella #414 (M4). Operator report, 2026-11-07.\n\n### Analysis (#592)\n- Reply and new MP share `ReplyComposerView`. The bar is a plain `VStack` child, not a `safeAreaInset` or a keyboard toolbar.\n- A new MP moves focus from recipient, to subject, to text. The bar stays enabled while the recipient field has focus, and a tap on it runs `focused = .text`, which steals focus.\n- This is the suspected cause of the bounce. It is a hypothesis: reproduce it first.\n\n### Fix\n- Anchor the bar to the keyboard: `safeAreaInset(edge: .bottom)` or the keyboard toolbar placement.\n- Enable it only while the text field has focus.\n- No layout jump when focus moves between fields, in both the reply and the new-MP composer.\n- Coordinate with #429 (swipe-down saves the draft), which edits the same file.\n\n### Tests\n- A model or view test that the bar is disabled unless the text has focus, and that a bar action never moves focus off the recipient or subject field.\n- Show that it fails without the change.\n\n### Mac check\n- New MP on iPhone with the keyboard up: recipient → subject → text, with no vertical jump.\n- Reply composer unchanged.\n- iPad with a hardware keyboard.\n\nRouting: Opus 5.5 writes, Fable 5.1 reviews (focus and keyboard layout). Claimed for `ext/francoisgn-composer-b`.",
