   "body": "## Reproduction (mac/m2-lead repro) 2026-11-07: the bounce comes from the return key, not from the bar\n\n**Build** `f9901d9` (origin/dev-swift). **Device**: iPhone 18 Pro simulator, iOS 27.0, portrait, software keyboard. A new MP composer, logged in. Nothing was sent: every run ended with Annuler → Supprimer le brouillon. Driven by a UI test while the simulator screen was recorded. The bar's position was read from every frame of the recording (the edge between the page and the bar, 3 px per pt). Harness notes: the build was signed ad hoc (`CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY=-`) instead of unsigned, because an unsigned build cannot use the keychain to log in. The runs with XCTest's `typeText` were checked again with taps on the on-screen keys, and the results below hold for those taps.\n\n| Action (new MP, keyboard up) | Bar position | Bounce? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Tap Gras while the **recipient** has focus | still at 502 pt | no. Focus jumps to the text, which gets `[b][/b]` |\n| Tap Gras while the **subject** has focus | still at 502 pt | no. Same focus jump |\n| Tap Gras while the text has focus | still at 502 pt | no |\n| Tap the recipient, subject and text fields in any order | still at 502 pt | no |\n| Type in the recipient, subject and text (on-screen keys) | still at 502 pt | no |\n| **Return key (\"suivant\") in the recipient** → focus goes to the subject | the keyboard and the bar **drop off screen and come back**, about 0.5–0.6 s | **yes** |\n| **Return key (\"suivant\") in the subject** → focus goes to the text | same drop and return | **yes** |\n\nEach return-key bounce was seen in two runs: once with `typeText(\"\\n\")` and once with a tap on the on-screen \"suivant\" key. A frame strip was checked by eye. The keyboard goes fully down, then slides back up with the bar.\n\n### What this says about the cloud's assumed cause\n- **The assumed cause is wrong.** A tap on a bar button while the recipient or subject has focus does **not** bounce.\n- What it does do: it moves focus to the text and inserts the tag there. That is a separate problem. Disabling the bar outside the text, as the issue proposes, fixes it.\n- **The bounce comes from `.onSubmit { focused = .subject }`** on the recipient (`ReplyComposerView.swift` `messageFields`), and the same pattern on the subject. The return key ends editing, so the keyboard starts to hide. Then the focus change brings it back.\n- Anchoring the bar with `safeAreaInset` or a keyboard toolbar will **not** stop this, because the keyboard itself goes away. The fix must keep the keyboard up while moving to the next field.\n- Candidates (not verified here):\n  - set the next focus without letting the field end editing;\n  - or handle return in UIKit (`textFieldShouldReturn` returning false, then `becomeFirstResponder` on the next field).\n- Test to add: the bar's position does not change across a return-key move from the recipient to the subject to the text. A UI test that records the screen can show this; a model test cannot.\n\nNot checked: a physical iPhone, the iPad with a hardware keyboard, and the reply composer, which has no recipient or subject field (no return-key move to test).\n",
